  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Three actually inspected exterior pictures (2025 complete front,2026 low front detail,older city overview) and standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. Mislabelled interior picture excluded from exterior evidence. No bespoke plans/surveys researched or reference photos redistributed. Hidden/current rear detail and exact height datum remain approximate.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_a%C3%A9rea_de_la_Catedral_metropolitana_de_S%C3%A3o_Paulo_13.jpg",
        "author": "ProtoplasmaKid",
        "date": "2025-11-29",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected complete elevated frontal photograph. Twin pale square Gothic towers with lower pointed window tiers, high recessed paired louver/glazing stages, corner buttress shafts/pinnacles, steep pale green octagonal copper spires and small crosses. Central broad pointed timber/glass entrance lies beneath a large circular geometric rose and steep triangular stone gable. Flanking smaller door/window fields and shallow figure niches. Pale green ribbed dome with small open lantern rises behind. Broad front stairs descend into Praça da Sé. Palm trees, street lamps and adjacent buildings excluded."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catedral_da_S%C3%A9_-_S%C3%A3o_Paulo,_Brasil.jpg",
        "author": "Helena Panzera",
        "date": "2026-02-07",
        "license": "CC0-1.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected low-angle front detail. Pale coursed masonry, tall pointed layered portal/window surrounds, large circular wheel/flower tracery rose, slender flanking lancets and shallow statues/niches. Square lower towers have tall pointed fields; upper stages have deep dark/louvered fields, small round oculi, triangular hoodlets and corner pinnacles. Warm photo lighting does not establish a yellow wall palette. Portal bases and spire tips are cropped."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catedral_da_S%C3%A9_-_Banespa.jpg",
        "author": "fotosedm.hpg.ig.com.br; individual photographer unspecified",
        "date": null,
        "license": "Attribution-required free-use permission recorded on Commons page",
        "observed": "Actually inspected older elevated city overview (first uploaded2006, rotated2017; capture date unspecified). Twin tall pale green spires rise before the much broader ribbed green dome and small lantern. Pointed gables/corner pinnacles and lower side/rear green roofs surround the dome. Base and much of the rear/side are obscured by neighboring buildings and trees. Supports broad forms only; hidden window rhythm, buttresses and current roof finish remain estimates."
      }
    ]
